kexts/       Builds against NVIDIA's open GPU kernel modules 620.70.06, MIT (with GPL-2.0 alternatives
             where noted), https://github.com/NVIDIA/open-gpu-kernel-modules
             (licenses/NVIDIA-open-gpu-kernel-modules-COPYING.txt).

NVK          Vulkan driver from Mesa, MIT (licenses/Mesa-license.rst). NullMoth's changes ship as patches.
             NAK's Rust crates (paste, proc-macro2, quote, rustc-hash, syn, unicode-ident; MIT and/or Apache-2.0): licenses/nvk-rust-crates.txt.

Vulkan loader  The Khronos Vulkan-Loader v1.4.367 (commit aa6dee8385afe4b2cc0152d086af2184743e16fd), built unmodified from source
             for x86_64 by build/build_vulkan_loader.sh and offered to applications by package/vulkan-for-apps.sh,
             Apache-2.0 (licenses/Vulkan-Loader-LICENSE.txt), https://github.com/KhronosGroup/Vulkan-Loader. Built against
             Vulkan-Headers v1.4.367 (commit 9fbc2a782ee3f8a4db64e7d991e23da75e893f44), Apache-2.0.

GSP firmware gsp_tu10x.bin, gsp_ga10x.bin and the matching ucode images are not part of this package. The installer
             (package/fw_fetch.sh) reads them, unmodified, from NVIDIA's own 620.70.06 Linux driver package downloaded
             to the user's Mac and checks each against a pinned SHA-256. They stay under NVIDIA's licence
             (licenses/NVIDIA-firmware-LICENCE.txt is the text that applies to those files).

kexts/NMGopFB  Finding the firmware framebuffer, checking it against the GPU's memory BARs and mapping it write-combined
             follow PrimeBridge by myvoow, https://github.com/myvoow/PrimeBridge (BootFramebuffer.cpp), MIT License,
             Copyright (c) 2026 myvoow (licenses/PrimeBridge-LICENSE.txt), whose author allowed this project to use and link it.
             The panel-provider design is NullMoth's own; PrimeBridge's patched NVRMFB is not used.

kexts/NMIntelFB  Panel brightness follows the method of WhateverXe's panel PWM (XELP::PanelPWM) by b00t0x,
             https://github.com/b00t0x/WhateverXe, BSD-3-Clause, Copyright (c) 2018 vit9696
             (licenses/WhateverXe-LICENSE.txt). Register layout from Linux i915/xe display headers, MIT.
             The hybrid-laptop sleep and wake replay (nm_hybrid_resume*.h: display core init, display clock, combo and Cx0 PHY
             sequences, link training, drive tables), the Type-C connect flow (nm_hybrid_tc.h), and the C20 PHY PLL tables
             (nm_hybrid_c20tables.h, copied value for value) are ported from the Linux kernel's i915/xe display driver
             (drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display), MIT, Copyright (c) Intel Corporation and the i915 contributors
             (licenses/Linux-i915-display-LICENSE.txt).
             No Apple driver code is used or shipped.

NMXAudio     The HD Audio controller and codec layers are FreeBSD's snd_hda (sys/dev/sound/pci/hda: hdac.c,
             hdaa.c, hdacc.c, hdaa_patches.c), BSD-2-Clause (licenses/FreeBSD-snd_hda-LICENSE.txt).
             Installed on macOS 26 only, where macOS has no HD Audio driver.

vendor/nvenc  Video encoders and decoders for NVIDIA's NVENC and NVDEC engines, offered to apps through VideoToolbox
             (libnvencvt.dylib). mickys/nvenc, https://github.com/mickys/nvenc, MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 mickys
             (licenses/mickys-nvenc-LICENSE.txt). The source is imported unchanged apart from one added
             function; vendor/nvenc/SOURCE lists the commit and the change. Builds against NVIDIA's MIT-licensed
             open-gpu-kernel-modules and open-gpu-doc headers and Apple's decoder interface as published in WebKit (BSD).

translator/  The Rust crates linked into the translator (bitflags, itoa, libc, memchr, serde, syn and others, all MIT and/or
             Apache-2.0, one Unlicense-or-MIT) keep their licences: licenses/translator-rust-crates.txt has each licence text.

dlss/        dlss/zstd is the Zstandard 1.5.6 reference decoder, BSD-3-Clause (licenses/zstd-LICENSE.txt); dlss/blake3 is BLAKE3 1.8.2 as
             vendored by Mesa, used under CC0 1.0 (licenses/BLAKE3-LICENSE-CC0.txt). The package carries no NVIDIA DLSS code: NVIDIA's
             DLSS runtimes, NGX core and nvJitLink are downloaded by the user's Mac from NVIDIA's public sources, checked against
             pinned hashes, and stay under NVIDIA's licences (package/dlss_fetch.sh).

air-runtime  LLVM (Apache-2.0 with LLVM exceptions) and Zstandard (BSD-3-Clause); their licence texts are in
             NVMTLDriver.bundle/Contents/Resources/air-runtime.

kexts/NVRMFB EDID override files and the opt-in smaller boot rasters follow an idea by mickys
             (https://github.com/mickys/nvidia-macos-driver, commit 9c023cd), proposed for this project in
             pull request 468 by GeekAudio. The implementation here is written independently.

kexts/NVRM   BAR1 placement is clipped to the range IOKit can describe and the aperture list is built before any
             PCI write (nvrm_bar_limits.h, placeLargeBar1). Community contribution: pull requests #431 (GeekAudio)
             and #473 (Giraffe12311), based on the bar-preflight experiment by yuanjing-hash.

Community ideas  The shared family-VRAM import cache and the browser surface-publication default follow ideas first
             published by mickys (https://github.com/mickys/nvidia-macos-driver, PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0) and
             proposed to this project by GeekAudio in pull requests 463 and 481. The code here is NullMoth's own.

kexts/NMHDA  Volume and mute controls for display audio sinks (nmhda_gain.h, nmhda_volume.cpp, boot argument nmhdavol=1)
             follow the idea published in emirercan3459/nullmoth-nvidia-audio (no licence file): give the sink's engine the
             standard level and mute controls and scale the samples it writes. The implementation here uses IOAudioFamily's
             public interface only and is NullMoth's own.

tools        The field census names Raptor Lake-U 8086:A7AC after the Intel Core 5 120U driver project by pongpan-bk
             (no licence file), which reported the id. Nothing of that project is used.

kexts/NMSMN  Opt-in (nmsmn=1) root-only access to the SMU mailbox registers of an AMD host bridge, so a power-limit tool can run.
             tools/ryzenadj-macos holds NullMoth's macOS layer for RyzenAdj v0.19.0 (FlyGoat/RyzenAdj, LGPL-3.0, commit
             ea71739b4a3e1a0a624dfd1c9c268a31cb2a4182), which upstream does not have; it is combined with the unmodified tag and
             its complete source is that folder plus the tag. Idea: LuneFlu/AMDHelper (no licence file).

Community ideas  The hybrid-laptop notes on the Intel panel (sleep leaves the display engine unlit, flat frames before a
             first image, a start-up delay) come from kitsuneislife/nmx-intel; they were handed to the hybrid work and nothing
             of that repository is used.

plugin       Opt-in VRAM working copies for buffers (nvmtl_shared_wc.h, NVMTL_SHARED_VRAM, NVMTL_MANAGED_OWNED_VRAM) follow
             ideas from pull request 524 by emretascii (owned staging memory for caller pages that cannot be imported, with the
             GPU working in VRAM). The code here is NullMoth's own.

nvk          nvk/nvk-upstream-nak.patch carries commits from the Mesa project (MIT licence), listed in the patch header.

kexts/NVRM, kexts/NVRMFB, plugin
             The notebook power budget (nvrmtgp, with the GPS and NVPCF _DSM families behind nvrmgps and nvrmnvpcf), the
             integrated-GPU panel proxy head (nvfbigpu) and the switches for the repeat pipeline bind and the encoder's
             sampler-variant memo (NVMTL_NO_PSO_SKIP, NVMTL_NO_SV_MEMO) follow ideas first published in
             watchthelight-labs/NvGfx (PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0), a fork of this project. The code here is NullMoth's own.
kexts/NMKbdBacklight  The keyboard backlight plugin follows the structure of VirtualSMC's SMCLightSensor plugin and builds
             against Lilu and the VirtualSMC SDK (acidanthera, BSD-3-Clause). The report layouts and method encodings it uses
             were read from the public Linux drivers hid-apple (Apple keyboard backlight reports), ideapad-laptop (Lenovo KBLC,
             HALS, SALS), thinkpad_acpi (MLCG, MLCS), dell-laptop and dell-smbios-wmi (Dell SMBIOS keyboard light calls), msi-ec (BeardOverflow/msi-ec, GPL-2.0: the source of the MSI firmware-string table facts and the setter encoding; our code is our own), hid-asus (drivers/hid/hid-asus.c: the ASUS N-KEY handshake and brightness
             feature reports, tools/asus), and OpenRazer (the Razer feature report, tools/razer), which are GPL-2.0, and from the ACPI tables of laptops whose owners sent
             them in. No code was copied from them; the code here is NullMoth's own.
